Bundled data and correction metadata

The small real-tissue demonstrators are derived from the source resources
documented in help("vignetteData"), with their original authors and studies
credited there. The native resource collection is published under CC BY 4.0 at
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22733262.

inst/extdata/mouse_brain_scalefactors.json preserves the Space Ranger factors
for V11L12-109_B1 from Vicari et al., Spatial Multimodal Analysis of
Transcriptomes and Metabolomes in Tissues, version 1:
https://doi.org/10.17632/w7nw4km7xd.1.
The source dataset's licence is CC BY-NC 3.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/.

inst/extdata/*_interactions_v1.rds are correction maps generated by SpaMTP.
They contain row indices and interaction labels, not pathway graphs. They
apply only to collections whose SHA-256 fingerprint matches. Source graphs
retain their database-specific terms, including KEGG, Reactome, WikiPathways
and SMPDB; SpaMTP's MIT code licence does not relicense those databases.
The accompanying pathway_interactions_provenance.csv identifies the source
URLs and checksums. See help("bundledResourceFiles") and the source-repository
recipe data-raw/rebuild_pathway_interactions.R.

